Wrote one row for Benjamin Allen / minimum-wage, coded chair = rung 1. Both passages (SB 3 bill text and the Senate Floor vote page) support it as a two-passage vote record: the operative CPI-indexing clause in Section 1182.12(c) matches rung 1's "tie it to the cost of living, so it rises automatically each year without new legislation" exactly, and Allen's Aye appears in the Senate Floor concurrence Ayes list (26–12), well outside the near-unanimous threshold. No quotes were available since the only evidence is records, not statements.
